        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0459" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg347"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No.493.11a/14.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Calhoun to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Kef erring to department’s telegraphic
                    instructions of May 7 regarding the presentation of claims by American citizens
                    for indemnification for losses incurred at Changsha, I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith for your information my letter of instruction to the consulate general
                    at Hankow on this matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Calhoun.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d345-a1.xml" xpointer="d345-a1"/>
